// Where the time actually goes: every outbound call, by type and target.
//
// `requests` says an endpoint was slow. This says what it was waiting on -
// Azure SQL, Service Bus, or an HTTP call - which is the difference between
// "the API is slow" and a fix.
//
// Ordered by totalMs, not by p99, and that ordering is the point. The slowest
// single dependency is rarely the one worth fixing; the one the system spends
// the most *aggregate* time inside is. A 5ms call made 40,000 times outranks a
// 3-second call made twice, and only a sum ranks them that way round.
//
// THE EXCLUSION BELOW IS NOT TIDYING. Run without it and the top two rows are
// the worker's Service Bus receivers at ~1,091,000 ms each - roughly eighteen
// minutes apiece, against a system that handled one message. That is not load.
// A message processor holds a long-poll receive open while it waits for work,
// and the SDK reports the whole wait as dependency duration, so an *idle*
// consumer accrues the largest number on the page by doing nothing at all.
//
// Ranking by aggregate time is correct for dependencies on the request path
// and actively misleading for a consumer's receive loop, because the two
// measure different things under the same column name: one is time spent
// working, the other is time spent waiting to be given work. Excluding the
// receive loop by name keeps the ranking answering the question it claims to.
dependencies
| where timestamp > ago(1h)
// The receive loop, and only the receive loop. Sends, completes, dead-letters
// and every other Service Bus operation stay in - they are real work on a real
// path. `ServiceBusReceiver.Receive*` is the idle wait.
| where name !startswith "ServiceBusReceiver.Receive"
    and name !startswith "ServiceBusProcessor.Receive"
| summarize
    calls    = count(),
    failures = countif(success == false),
    totalMs  = sum(duration),
    p50      = percentile(duration, 50),
    p99      = percentile(duration, 99)
  by cloud_RoleName, type, target, name
| extend failurePct = round(100.0 * failures / calls, 2)
| project cloud_RoleName, type, target, name, calls, failurePct,
          totalMs = round(totalMs, 0), p50 = round(p50, 1), p99 = round(p99, 1)
| order by totalMs desc
